				'- <strong>Paraklētos</strong> (Greek): helper, advocate; the Paraclete of John 14-16.',
				'- <strong>Q</strong>: the hypothetical sayings source shared by Matthew and Luke (German <em>Quelle</em>).',
				'- <strong>Synoptic</strong>: “seen together”; the gospels of Matthew, Mark and Luke.',
				'- <strong>Canon</strong>: the list of books accepted as scripture.',
				'- <strong>Ebionites</strong>: early Jewish followers of Jesus who kept the law.',
